# Audit exceptions — contract
#
# Read by scripts/ci/cargo-audit-gate.mjs (CI job "cargo audit — contract").
# The gate fails on every RustSec vulnerability that is not listed here.
# Informational advisories (unmaintained / unsound / yanked) are reported as
# warnings but do not fail CI, so they need no entry.
#
# Format — one exception per line:
#   <RUSTSEC-ID>: <reason> <tracking issue URL> [expires YYYY-MM-DD]
#
# A GitHub issue link is REQUIRED; entries without one, duplicates, and
# expired entries fail the gate. See docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md.
#
# Example:
#   RUSTSEC-2024-0001: Not reachable from wasm32 target https://github.com/MyFanss/MyFans/issues/1234 expires 2026-12-31

# Currently no exceptions — all vulnerabilities must be fixed before merge.
#
# Known informational warnings (not gated, kept here for context):
#   RUSTSEC-2024-0436 paste (unmaintained) — transitive via soroban-sdk 21.7.7;
#     compile-time macro only, no runtime surface. Clears when soroban-sdk is upgraded.
#   RUSTSEC-2026-0012 keccak (unsound) — only with the `asm` feature on ARMv8;
#     contracts compile to wasm32-unknown-unknown so the path is never exercised.
